","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22432472?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe","html_url":"https://github.com/neonmoe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-07T18:48:19Z","updated_at":"2025-07-07T18:48:19Z","body":"Rebased after making changes based on reviews, and updated the screenshots to match.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3046201155/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3049211734","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108356#issuecomment-3049211734","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108356","id":3049211734,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61v0dW","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-08T14:33:21Z","updated_at":"2025-07-08T14:33:21Z","body":"> I will approve after I get a second opinion from @allenwp \n\nThanks for the mention, I always appreciate it :)\n\nShould we wait until KhronosGroup/glTF-Blender-IO#2554 is merged before locking in the luminous efficacy value used (177.83)? Also, in the comment where this constant is described, it might be good to link this source PR or related source code in other repositories.\n\nI'd like to hear thoughts from @will-ca and @RevoluPowered who have already discussed some of this in #73624\n\nI would love to dive deep into this, but I don't have the time in the next while to familiarize myself with Blender and its standards.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3049211734/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3049960048","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108356#issuecomment-3049960048","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108356","id":3049960048,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61yrJw","user":{"login":"neonmoe","id":22432472,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDMyNDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22432472?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe","html_url":"https://github.com/neonmoe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neonmoe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-08T18:45:05Z","updated_at":"2025-07-08T18:57:50Z","body":"After writing out [this comment on the glTF-specific issue](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/73624#issuecomment-3046288978), I think this might actually be best fixed for physical light units by letting Blender export using the \"spec\" lighting mode, passing the glTF light intensity values to our intensity parameter (and multiplying spot and omnilights by 4*pi), and leaving the energy parameter as 1. Then Godot would be working according to the glTF spec, and any luminous efficacy related decisions would be up to Blender. Currently it'd export lights using 683lm/W, which would be a little bright compared to 177.82lm/W, but still definitely in a usable range, compared to passing the 683-scale values into the energy parameter (which gets multiplied by 1000lm or 100000lx due to the default intensity), as Godot is currently doing.\r\n\r\nThat'd also fix #73624.\r\n\r\nAnd once Blender switches to 177.83lm/W, Godot wouldn't need any changes to reflect that.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3049960048/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":